    usbStepsAlpine: '<li>Download Alpine Linux "Standard" or "Extended" (x86_64) from alpinelinux.org.</li><li>Write it to a USB stick with Rufus (default ISO mode, the stick stays writable). After balenaEtcher or dd the stick is read-only: put the file on a second USB stick (FAT32) instead.</li><li>Unpack the downloaded ZIP and copy caracal.apkovl.tar.gz to the root of the stick.</li><li>Connect the PC to the network with a cable, plug in the stick and the screen and boot from the stick.</li><li>Alpine installs itself on the disk (the disk is erased), reboots and installs CARACAL. The screen shows the progress; in 15–30 minutes the node appears in the device list.</li>',
